# agentline — machine-local service health list (line 4 of the status bar)
#
# Copy to ~/.claude/agentline-services.conf and list what this host runs.
# That file is gitignored on purpose: each machine keeps its own units, and the
# list never travels between machines.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#   <systemd-unit-name>:<Label>
#
#   - blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored
#   - if <Label> is omitted, the unit name is used as the label
#   - units that do not exist on this host are skipped silently, so the same
#     file can be copied between hosts without breaking the status bar
#
# systemd is Linux-only. On macOS the panel stays empty and line 4 simply omits
# it, so this file is harmless there.
#
# Override the location with $AGENTLINE_SERVICES if you need to.
#
# Examples:
#
#   nginx:Web
#   postgresql:DB
#   redis-server:Cache
#   docker:Docker
